/**
 * Rendered automatically on any resource page whose frontmatter sets
 * medicalDisclaimer: true. It is not optional and not dismissible, and the
 * schema is what decides it renders — not whoever writes the Markdown.
 */
---

<aside class="disc" role="note">
  <h2 class="disc__head">This is general information, not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing on this page is advice about you. It summarises published research for a general
    audience. Before changing how you eat or train — especially while dieting for a
    competition — talk to a qualified professional: your campus sports medicine service, a
    physician, or a registered dietitian.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are struggling with food, your body or your training, that is worth taking
    seriously and there is help.
    <a href="/resources/health">Health &amp; wellbeing has the resources</a>, starting with
    your campus counselling service.
  </p>
</aside>

